# ---- raw data & large scientific binaries (downloaded via scripts/, never committed) ----
data/**
!data/README.md
!data/pertadapt/
!data/pertadapt/official/
!data/pertadapt/official/PROVENANCE.md
outputs/
*.h5ad
*.h5
*.loom
*.npz
*.npy
# ...but keep the small deposited paper-backing arrays under results/_paper/
!results/_paper/*.npz
# ...and the 4 example format-demo bundles (they document the .npz layout; excluded from the census re-score)
!predictions/example/*.npz
# ...and the deposited compact per-stratum MEAN bundles (Pearson-Δ-exact, ~KB each) that back the
# 35-cell census, so `make reproduce-eval` recomputes the real per-(model,task) scores GPU-free
!predictions/C1/*.npz
!predictions/C2/*.npz
!predictions/C3/*.npz
!predictions/C4/*.npz
!predictions/C5/*.npz
# ...and the directories this revision's re-runs deposit into. The allowlist named only C1-C5, so a
# fresh clone was missing 567 of the 1,401 bundles census_bundle_manifest.csv points at -- every
# native re-run (v2_native), the T2 metric-metadata correction (C2_metric_aligned) and the cells
# deposited at the predictions/ root. The availability statement promises a reader can re-score the
# deposit; without these they cannot. scripts/check_deposit_completeness.py fails the build if the
# manifest ever names a bundle git does not track again.
!predictions/v2_native/*.npz
!predictions/C2_metric_aligned/*.npz
!predictions/*.npz
# The chemCPA T5u provenance gate replays the census bundle from the three seed outputs that
# produced it. They used to live outside the repo, so `make check` died on a fresh clone.
!provenance/chemcpa/*.npz
*.pkl
*.rds
*.mtx
*.mtx.gz
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.parquet

